{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.Gen3MesonPhiHeckeSeifert","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.Gen3MesonPhiHeckeSeifert","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.Gen3.phiMassRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.Gen3.phiMassRatio","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert.lean#L55-L58","doc":"The third-generation meson mass ratio formula:\nm_φ/m_π = χ^{(2,1)}(σ₁⁷) × (15/7)². ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert","label":"prop:gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.Gen3.chi_21_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.Gen3.chi_21_odd","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert.lean#L47-L53","doc":"For odd n, χ^{(2,1)}(σ₁ⁿ) = qⁿ - q⁻ⁿ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.Gen3.chi_21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.Gen3.chi_21","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert.lean#L42-L45","doc":"Hecke character χ^{(2,1)}(σ₁ⁿ) = qⁿ + (-q⁻¹)ⁿ for the standard\nrepresentation of H₃(q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.Gen3.seifert_ratio_T27_T23","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.Gen3.seifert_ratio_T27_T23","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert.lean#L29-L40","doc":"Seifert volume ratio V_S(T(2,7)) / V_S(T(2,3)) = 15/7, over any field\nin which 2, 3, 7 are invertible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.Gen3.seifertEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.Gen3.seifertEuler","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert.lean#L25-L27","doc":"Seifert Euler number of T(2,n): e = 1 - 1/2 - 1/n = (n-2)/(2n). ","signatureChunk":0}]}